messages:
Eli: Proposal: break the big structured-output page into two focused PRs to speed reviews. PR A = schemas + static examples. PR B = runtime parsing patterns + SDK snippets + fallback heuristics. I'll open both and assign owners.

Maria: I can own PR A (schemas + examples). I'll also add compact examples for nullable arrays and union arrays. Plan to move the examples into docs/schemas/ with frontmatter so the sidebar picks them up.

Cheng: I'll take PR B (parsing + SDK). Intend to add: 1) tryParse + envelope fallback code for SDK 4.x, 2) a small regex fallback snippet, 3) notes about when to prefer function-calling vs structured output.

Sam: prefer moving SDK snippets to a single snippets/ directory under docs/parsers so we can import them into other pages. Also we should add a short migration snippet comparing SDK 3.x and 4.x function call shapes.

Alisa: I can do the link audit. There's some legacy links in docs/structured-output/ referencing examples that will move. I can submit a redirects-only PR if that helps unblock merging.

Ben: small lint nit in one of the examples: fenced code blocks missing language tag and a JSON block with trailing comma. I'll paste the failing block in PR comments.

DocsBot: Heads-up: add 'migration-notes' label if examples change user-facing return shapes. Also run the link-checker before merging.

Eli: timeline: aim to have both PRs draft-ready tomorrow, land both by Friday. If link PR is required, Alisa, can you land that before schema PR merge?

Alisa: yep, will open the redirect map PR within the hour. I'll include a small changelog blurb.

Maria: opened PR A: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/861 with initial commit + examples moved. Left TODOs for compact nullable-array examples and a note to add JSON Schema validation sample.

Cheng: draft PR B pushed: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/862. Includes SDK 4.x parse envelope snippet and a tryParse fallback example. Need someone to sanity-check the compatibility notes for function-calling.

Sam: reviewing PR 861 now. I'll flag any doc-style nits but major structure looks good.

Ben: posted the exact lint error in PR 861 comments. Suggest running `prettier --check` locally.

Eli: thank you. Cheng, for the SDK snippet keep it very small. Example idea:```js
// SDK 4.x: parse envelope fallback
try {
  const out = JSON.parse(responseText);
  return out;
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: minimal regex extraction for common key
  const m = /\"result\"\s*:\s*\"([^\"]+)\"/.exec(responseText);
  return m ? {result: m[1]} : {raw: responseText, parseError: true};
}
```

Cheng: pulled that in and added comments about when this fallback is acceptable (best-effort, not for PII).

Alisa: redirect PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/863. It includes a short redirect map and updates to the sidebar.

Maria: merged PR 861 (schemas + examples). Left a small follow-up to address Ben's lint nit.

Cheng: merging PR 862 now after Sam's review. Added the migration blurb comparing SDK 3.x -> 4.x function call payload shapes (kept terse).

Alisa: merged redirect PR 863 and updated the changelog entry.

Eli: sweet. Can someone add a one-line release-notes blurb in the release-notes draft? Something like: "Docs: split structured output guidance into schema and parsing sections; added SDK 4.x parsing fallback examples and redirect map."

Sam: added the blurb. Closing thread. :tada:
